{
  "protocol": "At each flight tick, H, a unit rail-controlled mass translation, H, a programmed compensating unit-stroke sequence on the same ring, and one site stream. Use C_s=exp(-i*s*theta*sigma_x) in the mass frame. Real H at launch prepares +X. Native position and rail reads ignore the diagonal change of spin and force frames.",
  "hardware": "Two-dimensional cylinder (x,y) with a finite rail, nearest-neighbour base +/-1 and local sheet \u00b11 permutations; local H and real signed readout. At horizon T, force vector stride bound Qmax=ceil(|f|cT/mu)+1. Allocate subslots, including padding for different q. If base pitch is c*tau, retain base speed c per full tick. When moves occupy distinct clock subslots the strict microstep propagation bound is larger by a FIXED factor; to use a single speed cap v include fixed subslot overhead or allow simultaneous base/sheet shifts with bounded product-metric velocity. Site placement, a distinct physical sheet coordinate per local base mode, joint phase preparation and synchronized translated programs are required. Ring circumference at sheet pitch O(tau) is O(epsilon); a fixed circumference has a different physical resource cost.",
  "comparison": "The scalar uniform force and the exact vector representation agree up to exp(-i*n*h*x) at the output. Between the rounded and exact vector flights, pending z rotation s*theta*(Q_n-h*n(n+1)/(2*theta)) cancels the incremental vector-phase discrepancy. Conjugating the small mass coin by the pending phase costs <=2*abs(sin(s*theta)*sin(r)). For |s|=1 the uniform operator norm error is <=theta/2+2*n*abs(sin(theta))*sin(theta/2); tau=o(epsilon\u00b2) suffices. Per-tick rounding without accumulating the phase remainder need not converge; small force max |f|T<mu/(2c) rounds every desired stroke to zero.",
  "limitations": "The selected character pair is an input, and a localized physical sheet does not have this purity. Uniform field is preprogrammed as a common time-dependent local phase; scalar-force address transport, an unknown remote force source, spin tomography in a fixed transverse basis, and nonlocal spatial-coherence reads are distinct tasks. Finite M and bounded transfer O(1) strokes require a specifiable finite field range and horizon or new clock controls.",
