  "resource_counts": "For physical base interval of width L_x, about (L_x/(c*tau))*M cylinder sites carry the rails. Given a rational h/theta, exact integer schedules can be preloaded identically at each base site or generated with a clock and remainder. Counter bit operations are not instantaneous nearest-neighbour primitives: a table of O(T/tau) settings, or a clockwork and its cycle time, is a supplied resource. The real folded character projector has diagonal 2/M, so a sheet state supported on A sites has pair mass at most 2*A/M even with unresolved ancillas. A bounded-speed preparation from one site needs order M*sheet_pitch time for near purity; this is a lower bound and not a construction from only synchronized Hadamards.",
